  "adaptation": {
    "semantic": "The number sense and the time sense (*a second*, one sixtieth of a minute) are translated with different words in many languages; do not use one word for both.",
    "grammar": null,
    "culture": "In American English the *first floor* is at street level, so the *second floor* is one floor up. In British English the *first floor* is already one floor up, so the *second floor* is two floors up.",
